//==
// # Element quality: types
//
// Shape metrics of single elements and the thresholds they are reported against. Quality is
// measured and reported, never promised: with the boundary locked to the edge polylines no
// triangulator can guarantee an angle bound (research/MESHING-REQUIREMENTS.md, finding 8). A
// quality threshold failing is an Info finding (SPEC-DSL.md section 4); the two shape conditions
// that break the mesh as a surface, a non-convex quad and a fold, are laws of Error severity.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Metrics
//  - Thresholds

//==
// # Metrics

// The shape metrics of one triangle (research/MESHING-REQUIREMENTS.md 1.3). MinAngle and MaxAngle
// are its smallest and largest interior angles. RadiusRatio is circumradius over twice inradius,
// R / (2 r): 1 for an equilateral triangle, larger otherwise (Euler's inequality R >= 2 r).
// AspectRatio is (sqrt(3) / 6) times the longest side over the inradius (Frey and George), also 1
// for an equilateral triangle. MinAltitude is twice the area over the longest side, the length the
// degeneracy test compares with the model's tolerance. A degenerate triangle has zero inradius and
// so an infinite or undefined RadiusRatio and AspectRatio, which fail every threshold.
type TriangleQuality
    implements IValue
{
    MinAngle: Angle;
    MaxAngle: Angle;
    RadiusRatio: Number;
    AspectRatio: Number;
    MinAltitude: Number;
}

// The shape metrics of one quadrilateral (research/MESHING-REQUIREMENTS.md 1.3 and 5.4).
// MinAngle and MaxAngle are its smallest and largest corner angles. AngleDefect is 2 pi minus the
// corner angle sum: 0 exactly when the quad is planar and convex (research/VALIDATION-MATH.md 4.5).
// Skew is |cos A|, A the angle between the two lines that join the midpoints of opposite sides: 0
// for a rectangle. WarpCosine is the smaller, over the two diagonal splits, of the cosine of the
// angle between the normals of the split's two triangles: 1 for a planar quad. ScaledJacobian is
// the smallest, over the corners, of the corner's cross product along the unit mid-plane normal
// (the direction of (C - A) x (D - B)) over the product of the corner's two side lengths: 1 for a
// rectangle, at most 0 at a reflex or folded corner. MinAltitude is the smallest altitude of the
// four triangles of both splits.
type QuadQuality
    implements IValue
{
    MinAngle: Angle;
    MaxAngle: Angle;
    AngleDefect: Angle;
    Skew: Number;
    WarpCosine: Number;
    ScaledJacobian: Number;
    MinAltitude: Number;
}

//==
// # Thresholds

// The quality thresholds elements are reported against. CubitAcceptable gives the "acceptable"
// ranges of the Cubit manual (research/MESHING-REQUIREMENTS.md 1.3), finite-element conventions
// cited as a common reference, not requirements of any exchange format. Quad corner angles carry no
// threshold: the research names no source for one.
type MeshQualityThresholds
    implements IValue
{
    TriangleMinAngle: Angle;
    TriangleMaxAngle: Angle;
    MaxRadiusRatio: Number;
    MaxAspectRatio: Number;
    MaxQuadSkew: Number;
    MinQuadWarpCosine: Number;
    MaxQuadAngleDefect: Angle;
    MinQuadScaledJacobian: Number;
}
